Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang — crime of职务侵占

Prosecutor: Fujian Provincial Xiamen City People's Procuratorate.

Defendant: Zhang Zhengui, male, 23 years old, a native of Putian City, Fujian Province, formerly a gatekeeper at Fujian Provincial Xiamen City Xiangyu Storage and Transportation Co., Ltd., arrested on June 4, 1999.

Defense Counsel: Du Dehai, lawyer of Fujian Provincial Xiamen Tianyi Law Firm.

Defendant: Huang Wenzhang, male, 30 years old, a native of Longhai City, Fujian Province, formerly a preliminary inspector at Fujian Provincial Xiamen City Xiangyu Shengshi Container Co., Ltd., arrested on June 4, 1999.

Defense Counsel: Li Mingquan, lawyer of Fujian Provincial Xiamen Jianchang Law Firm.

Fujian Provincial Xiamen City People's Procuratorate filed a public prosecution with Fujian Provincial Xiamen Intermediate People's Court against the defendants Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang for the crime of embezzlement.

The indictment alleged: After the defendant Zhang Zhengui was employed as a gatekeeper at Fujian Provincial Xiamen City Xiangyu Storage and Transportation Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as Storage and Transportation Company), he took advantage of his position of being responsible for inspecting and watching over container cargo in the customs inspection yard of Xiangyu Bonded Zone, and colluded with the defendant Huang Wenzhang to steal three container cargos deposited by Xiamen Xiangyu Nanguang Minmetals Import and Export Trade Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as Minmetals Company) in the customs inspection yard. The containers contained 1,860 cases of "Hualong" brand polyester processed yarn (i.e., polyester filament yarn). The total value of the containers, cargo, and the three chassis stolen together was RMB 659,878. Zhang Zhengui, as a person entrusted by a state-owned company to manage state-owned assets, took advantage of his position and colluded with the defendant Huang Wenzhang to commit embezzlement by stealing company property under his custody. Their conduct violated Article 382, paragraphs 2 and 3, and Article 25 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, jointly constituting the crime of embezzlement. The amount jointly embezzled by Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang was particularly huge, causing great losses to the state, and the circumstances of the crime were particularly serious, which should be punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 383, item 1 of the Criminal Law. A public prosecution was specially filed, and a judgment according to law was requested.

The prosecuting authority submitted the following evidence to the court: case reporting materials, case filing materials, property seizure records, property restitution records, appraisal report, identity certificates of the two defendants, temporary labor contracts, business license of the Storage and Transportation Company, articles of association, contractual operation agreement, operating regulations of the inspection yard, fee approval document from Xiamen Price Bureau, payment card for the stolen containers, witness testimony, and photos of the scene, etc.

The defendant Zhang Zhengui confessed to the facts alleged in the indictment. At trial, his own defense and the defense opinions of his defense counsel were: 1. The goods in the inspection yard were managed by the Xiangyu Bonded Zone, and the Storage and Transportation Company for which Zhang Zhengui worked was only responsible for collecting fees and releasing vehicles, not for verifying who the owner of the goods was. Therefore, there was a site lease relationship between the Storage and Transportation Company and the owner of the goods, and the stolen goods were not state-owned assets under the custody of the Storage and Transportation Company, nor could Zhang Zhengui become a person entrusted by the Storage and Transportation Company to manage state-owned assets. According to the internal regulations of the Storage and Transportation Company, Zhang Zhengui's duties as a gatekeeper were to maintain vehicle order during the day and to collect fees and release vehicles on behalf of others at night. He did not have the right or obligation to manage, so it could not be said that he took advantage of his position. His conduct was at most secret theft. The indictment charging him with the crime of embezzlement was a mischaracterization of the crime. 2. Regarding the positions and roles of the two defendants in this case, contacting the tow truck driver and disposing of the stolen goods were all operations carried out by the defendant Huang Wenzhang, and Zhang Zhengui was not aware of them. Therefore, Zhang Zhengui was an accessory, also a first-time offender, and had a good attitude of repentance after the crime. He requested a lighter punishment.

The defendant Huang Wenzhang also had no objection to the facts alleged in the indictment. The defense opinions of his defense counsel were: 1. From the actual circumstances of this case, the work at the customs inspection yard—entry registration, opening containers, loading and unloading, checking and releasing—was only general labor and did not have a management nature. The defendant Zhang Zhengui was only a gatekeeper, and his work was even less managerial in nature. His status did not conform to the "entrusted management" referred to in the Criminal Law and could not constitute the subject of the crime of embezzlement. In addition, the object of the crime in this case was property owned by Minmetals Company, of which 50% was foreign investment, and thus did not fall within the object of the crime of embezzlement—state-owned property. Therefore, the conduct of the two defendants jointly stealing the property of Minmetals Company should be characterized as the crime of职务侵占 rather than the crime of embezzlement. 2. The two defendants did not know in advance what was in the containers or how much they were worth, indicating that the object of the crime in this case was not specific, and the social harmfulness of the defendants' criminal conduct was relatively small, warranting a lighter punishment. 3. The stolen goods in this case were bonded goods, and their value should be calculated based on the price in the bonded market. 4. In the joint crime, the criminal intent was initiated by Zhang Zhengui, and the theft of the containers was also mainly carried out by Zhang Zhengui. The defendant Huang Wenzhang only performed auxiliary tasks and should be deemed an accessory in this case. Moreover, Huang Wenzhang had circumstances that could warrant a lighter punishment, such as having a good attitude of admitting guilt and assisting the public security organs in recovering most of the stolen goods. He requested a lighter punishment.

Xiamen Intermediate People's Court found after trial:

The defendant Zhang Zhengui, by signing a temporary labor contract with the state-owned Storage and Transportation Company, was employed as a gatekeeper at the customs inspection yard operated by the Storage and Transportation Company under a contractual arrangement. During his shifts, he was responsible for the safety of containers and goods in the inspection yard, releasing vehicles based on the payment cards held by drivers, and at night, he also performed duties such as time-checking and fee collection for container vehicles entering and leaving the yard on behalf of business clerks and accounting clerks. During his employment, Zhang Zhengui repeatedly harbored the evil idea of gathering others to jointly steal containers from the inspection yard. After getting acquainted with the defendant Huang Wenzhang, who was working as a preliminary inspector at Xiamen Xiangyu Shengshi Container Co., Ltd., the two conspired and planned the crime.

On April 29, 1999, Minmetals Company transported six container cargos for export into the customs inspection yard for inspection. That day, it was Zhang Zhengui's shift. Zhang Zhengui, as agreed with the defendant Huang Wenzhang, notified Huang to contact a tow truck to commit the theft. At around 7:00 p.m. that day, Huang Wenzhang, along with the tow truck he had arranged, went to the customs inspection yard. With Zhang Zhengui's cooperation, they stole three container cargos (container numbers NE-WU5111199, NEWU5111120, NEWU5111218, containing 1,860 cases of polyester filament yarn) along with three chassis (total value RMB 659,878) out of the inspection yard. Using the stolen cargo release documents of Xiamen Xiangyu Shengshi Container Company, Huang Wenzhang transported the containers out of the bonded zone gate and then drove them overnight to Gangwei Town, Longhai City, preparing to dispose of the stolen goods. After Huang left, Zhang Zhengui went to the gatehouse of the bonded zone and, taking advantage of the duty officer's inattention, stole and destroyed the cargo release documents and the cargo exit registration forms for the three containers.

The next morning, the Storage and Transportation Company reported the case. On May 3, the two defendants were arrested by the public security organs. The defendant Huang Wenzhang confessed the whereabouts of the stolen goods and led the police to Dongyuan Village, Xiangzhi Town, Shishi City, where they recovered the three stolen containers, three chassis, and 999 cases of polyester filament yarn, and to Gangwei Town, Longhai City, where they recovered 229 cases of polyester filament yarn. At the same time, the public security organs also retrieved 345 cases of polyester filament yarn that had been seized by the Gangwei Town Industrial and Commercial Office during Huang Wenzhang's transfer of the stolen goods. The above stolen goods have all been returned to the victim unit, and 287 cases of polyester filament yarn worth RMB 76,715 remain unrecovered.

The above facts are confirmed by the following evidence:

1. The confessions of the defendants Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang during the court trial, which mutually corroborated the entire process from Zhang Zhengui's initiation of the criminal intent to the joint conspiracy and the commission of the crime;
2. Three payment cards for inspection at the customs inspection yard of Xiangyu Bonded Zone, confirming that at 3:29 p.m. on April 29, three container cargos with numbers 5111199, 5111120, and 5111218 were transported into the customs inspection yard by Minmetals Company, and were transported out at 7:54 p.m. that day, corroborating the confessions of the two defendants on this point;
3. The theft report, the public security organ's criminal case acceptance registration form, and case filing form, confirming the specific process of Minmetals Company reporting the theft of the three containers through Cai Zhiqiang of the Storage and Transportation Company, and confirming that the name, specifications, and quantity of the stolen goods, as well as the numbers of the stolen containers and chassis, matched the recovered stolen goods, and corroborated the relevant confessions of the two defendants;
4. The public security organ's explanation of the arrest of Huang Wenzhang and Zhang Zhengui, confirming that the two were arrested at Gao's residence based on a report by Gao Anhui and Gao Yafa, and were transferred to the Criminal Police Brigade of Huli Sub-bureau, Xiamen Public Security Bureau;
5. The records of recovery, restitution, and return of stolen goods, confirming that after the incident, Huang Wenzhang led the police to recover stolen goods in Shishi, Gangwei, and other places, corroborating Huang Wenzhang's confession on this point;
6. The appraisal report from Xiamen Price Office, confirming: based on the evaluation of the stolen items, each case of 33 kg, specification 300D polyester filament yarn, at the median market price of RMB 8,100 per ton, 1,860 cases total 61.38 tons, valued at RMB 497,178; three high-cube containers, valued at 65% of new, worth RMB 70,200; three container chassis, valued at 50% of new, worth RMB 92,500. The total of the three items is RMB 659,878;
7. The business license, articles of association, contractual operation agreement, and the Price Bureau's fee approval document of the Storage and Transportation Company, confirming that the Storage and Transportation Company is a joint-stock company invested and established by two wholly state-owned companies, that the Storage and Transportation Company has a warehousing business scope, and is responsible for the custody of goods stored in the customs inspection yard under its contractual operation;
8. The household registration materials of Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang, confirming their dates of birth;
9. The temporary labor contract signed between the Storage and Transportation Company and Zhang Zhengui, and the employee resume of the Storage and Transportation Company, confirming that Zhang Zhengui was employed by the Storage and Transportation Company to perform gatekeeping labor;
10. Certificates issued by the Storage and Transportation Company, gatekeeper duties for the inspection yard, operating regulations for the inspection platform, and other documentary evidence, confirming that Zhang Zhengui's duties as gatekeeper of the inspection yard were: to release vehicles leaving the inspection yard based on paid payment cards, to ensure the safety of goods in the yard, and at night, to perform time-checking and fee collection for container vehicles entering and leaving the yard on behalf of business clerks and accounting clerks;
11. Testimony of witness Cai Zhiqiang, Assistant General Manager of the Storage and Transportation Company, and Cai Minghuang, Deputy General Manager of Xiangyu Group Freight Company, confirming that the Storage and Transportation Company bore the responsibility for the safety custody of goods in the inspection yard;
12. Testimony of witness Wang Shutao, Manager of the Business Department of Xiangyu Construction Company, confirming that the inspection yard was developed and funded by the Construction Company and then handed over to the Storage and Transportation Company for contractual operation, responsible for the management of goods in the yard. This testimony corroborated the testimonies of Cai Zhiqiang and Cai Minghuang;
13. Testimony of witnesses Zhu Jineng, Zhang Wenling (business clerks at the inspection yard), and Wang Weiling (accounting clerk at the inspection yard), not only confirming the work procedure for releasing vehicles at the inspection yard, but also confirming that on the morning of April 30, after coming on duty, Zhang Zhengui handed over to them three payment cards and RMB 450, and informed them that the three containers of Minmetals Company had been taken away by the owner. The three testimonies corroborated each other and were consistent with other evidence and Zhang Zhengui's confession;
14. Testimony of witness Zhang Huihong, an employee of Minmetals Company, confirming that on April 29, the company transported six containers into the inspection yard, and the next day found that three were missing, consistent with Zhang Zhengui's confession;
15. Testimony of witness Pan Zhaoxiang, confirming that Zhang Zhengui had twice (in July and November 1998) proposed to him the idea of jointly stealing containers from the inspection yard, but he did not agree. This testimony corroborated Zhang Zhengui's confession;
16. Testimony of witness Wei Lizhong, a duty officer at the bonded zone gate, confirming that at around 7:30 p.m., 8:00 p.m., and 9:00 p.m. on April 29, Zhang Zhengui came to the duty booth where he was on duty three times to play, and at around 8:00 p.m., Zhang even filled in for him for a while on duty; on that day, vehicles were inspected and registered before being released, and the release documents and registration forms were placed on the desk in the duty room. After the incident, it was found that the three container release documents of Shengshi Company from the evening of April 29 and the relevant registration forms were missing or torn out. This testimony corroborated Zhang Zhengui's confession;
17. Testimony of witnesses Wu Weiping, Chen Qianyuan, Huang Songjie, Zheng Baosheng, and Zhou Jiansheng (dispatchers and drivers of Xiamen Yuntong Container Company), confirming that at around 7-8 p.m. on April 29, a young man with a Longhai accent asked them to transport three containers from the inspection yard to Gangwei, Longhai, and the exit procedures were handled by the young man, who asked the container trucks to detour through Shengshi Company before leaving the bonded zone gate. These witness testimonies not only corroborated each other but also corroborated the confessions of Huang Wenzhang and Zhang Zhengui;
18. Testimony of witnesses Gao Anhui and Gao Yafa, confirming that on the afternoon of April 29, Huang Wenzhang asked Gao Anhui to contact a tow truck to transport containers from the bonded zone. Gao Anhui then contacted a Xiamen tow truck driver through Gao Guojin and gave the driver's phone number to Huang Wenzhang, asking Huang to contact him directly. After that, Huang Wenzhang transported three containers to Gangwei Town. On May 1, through Gao Yafa's contact, Huang Wenzhang and Gao Yafa transported the three containers and cargo to Jinjiang for storage. On May 3, after learning that the goods were stolen from the bonded zone by Huang, they immediately reported to the police station. The testimonies of the two witnesses corroborated each other and were consistent with part of Huang Wenzhang's confession;
19. Testimony of witness Jiang Lian'gen from Dajing Village, Gangwei Town, confirming that on the evening of April 30, Huang Wenzhang transported 229 cases of polyester filament yarn and stored them at his home. This testimony was consistent with part of Huang Wenzhang's confession;
20. Testimony of witness Lin Bangji from Dongyuan Village, Xiangzhi Town, Shishi City, confirming that around May 1, a person nicknamed "Yachou" and several young men from other places transported some goods packed in cartons and stored them at his home; according to Yachou, they were for weaving. This testimony corroborated part of Huang Wenzhang's confession and the testimonies of witnesses Gao Anhui and Gao Yafa;
21. Photos of the scene, stolen containers, cargo, tow trucks, and the cargo exit registration book of the bonded zone duty police team were attached to the case file.

All the above evidence was cross-examined in court, and the two defendants had no objection. It can be used as the basis for finding the facts of this case.

Xiamen Intermediate People's Court held:

The evidence in this case confirms that after the Storage and Transportation Company took over the contractual operation of the customs inspection yard, it had the responsibility for the custody of goods entering the yard. Therefore, during the period when the goods were under the custody of the Storage and Transportation Company, they were deemed to be property owned by the Storage and Transportation Company. Article 382, paragraph 2 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China provides: "Any person entrusted by a State organ, State-owned company, enterprise, institution, or people's organization to manage or operate State-owned property who, by taking advantage of his position, embezzles, steals, defrauds, or otherwise illegally appropriates the State-owned property shall be deemed to have committed the crime of embezzlement." Since the Storage and Transportation Company is a joint-stock company invested and established by two state-owned companies, although the property under its custody could be classified as state-owned property under its management, the defendant Zhang Zhengui was only an employee hired by the company, performing the labor of watching over the inspection yard. His status was that of a general worker, without management rights over the goods in the yard. He neither belonged to "persons engaged in public service in a company, enterprise, or other state-owned unit" nor to "persons entrusted to manage or operate state-owned property." Therefore, he could not be the subject of the crime of embezzlement. Consequently, the prosecution's allegation that the defendants' conduct constituted the crime of embezzlement was a mischaracterization and should be corrected. The arguments of Zhang Zhengui, Huang Wenzhang, and their defense counsels regarding the improper characterization of the crime in this case can be adopted.

Article 271 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China provides: "Any employee of a company, enterprise, or other unit who, by taking advantage of his position, unlawfully takes possession of the property of his own unit, if the amount is relatively large, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention; if the amount is huge, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years and may also be sentenced to confiscation of property." The defendant Zhang Zhengui, by signing a temporary labor contract with the Storage and Transportation Company, was employed as a gatekeeper at the customs inspection yard operated by the Storage and Transportation Company under a contractual arrangement. During his employment, Zhang Zhengui took advantage of his position of watching over the goods in the yard, checking and releasing vehicles, and performing time-checking and fee collection for container vehicles entering and leaving the yard on behalf of business clerks and accounting clerks. He conspired with the defendant Huang Wenzhang, colluding internally and externally to jointly steal the containers under the custody of the Storage and Transportation Company. Their conduct violated the provisions of Article 271, paragraph 1 of the Criminal Law and constitutes the crime of职务侵占. In accordance with Article 25 of the Criminal Law, Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang committed a joint crime, and the amount involved was huge. Goods worth RMB 76,715 remain unrecovered to date, and they should be punished according to law.

In order to achieve their common criminal purpose, in this crime, Zhang Zhengui took advantage of his position to allow the tow truck to enter the customs inspection yard and, after the theft was successful, allowed the tow truck to leave the inspection yard. Additionally, both defendants separately engaged in acts not taking advantage of their positions, such as using the stolen cargo release documents to transport the containers out of the bonded zone gate and destroying the cargo release documents and cargo exit registration forms kept in the gatehouse. The success of this crime had a necessary causal relationship with Zhang Zhengui's taking advantage of his position. The acts of the two defendants not taking advantage of their positions occupied a secondary role. Therefore, the crime should be characterized as职务侵占. In this joint crime, both defendants were indispensable and played equivalent roles, so it is not appropriate to distinguish between a principal offender and an accessory. The defense counsel's argument for Zhang Zhengui that he had no right or duty to manage the goods and therefore could not have taken advantage of his position, at most constituting secret theft, and the arguments of the defense counsels for Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang that their respective clients were accessories in this case are inconsistent with the facts and are not adopted.

The Supreme People's Court, in Article 5 of the "Interpretation on Several Issues Concerning the Specific Application of Law in the Trial of Theft Cases" (Fa Shi [1998] No. 4), provides that the value of stolen import and export goods shall be calculated based on the median market retail price of commodities in the circulation field. Therefore, the defense argument of Zhang Zhengui's defense counsel that the value of the stolen goods in this case should be calculated based on the bonded goods price lacks a legal basis and is not adopted.

Given that both defendants had a good attitude of admitting guilt after being brought to justice, and that the defendant Huang Wenzhang also assisted the public security organs in recovering most of the stolen goods, thereby compensating for most of the victim's economic losses, both may be given a lighter punishment as appropriate. The requests of the defense counsels for Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang for a lighter punishment may be adopted. Accordingly, Xiamen Intermediate People's Court hereby adjudges:

1. The defendant Zhang Zhengui is convicted of the crime of职务侵占 and sentenced to nine years' imprisonment, with confiscation of property of RMB 10,000; the defendant Huang Wenzhang is convicted of the crime of职务侵占 and sentenced to eight years' imprisonment, with confiscation of property of RMB 10,000;
2. The criminal proceeds of the two defendants amounting to RMB 76,715 shall be further recovered and returned to the victim unit.

After the first instance judgment was pronounced, the defendants Zhang Zhengui and Huang Wenzhang did not appeal, and the prosecuting authority did not lodge a protest. The judgment has become legally effective.
